ith the whole wrapper Self, not its inner T. These are distinct from primitive/cross-endian From conversions and add no primary mappings. The Rust wrapper nominal types remain distinct even though their extracted single-field views are reducible aliases. Six additional conditional compiler-inlined caller contracts cover Into<U>, TryInto<U> and TryFrom<U> for each original wrapper. Into delegates exactly to the supplied U:From<Self> callback; TryInto delegates exactly to U:TryFrom<Self>, retaining arbitrary associated Error values. For TryFrom<U>, the supplied U:Into<Self> callback is bound into Ok with Never error type. Each equation retains modeled callback failure/divergence rather than assuming success or termination. Payload T is distinct from whole-wrapper Self; U is destination for Into/TryInto and source for TryFrom.",
